WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.002 --> 00:00:13.624
I'm here in Egypt, standing on the Giza Plateau, which is known for its massive pyramids.

2
00:00:14.564 --> 00:00:19.625
The pyramid closest to me is the Pyramid of Khafre, named for the pharaoh who built it.

3
00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.487
The farther one is called the Great Pyramid of Giza.

4
00:00:24.427 --> 00:00:27.688
The Pharaoh Khufu—Khafre's father—built that one.

5
00:00:28.652 --> 00:00:33.793
You might find this hard to believe, but these pyramids were built over four thousand years ago.

6
00:00:34.854 --> 00:00:36.954
Hidden in the gray dawn, there's something else.

7
00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:38.535
Do you see it?

8
00:00:38.895 --> 00:00:40.615
It's the back of a massive head!

9
00:00:41.016 --> 00:00:44.036
You're looking at the Great Sphinx of Giza!

10
00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:47.497
You've probably already heard of the Great Sphinx of Giza.

11
00:00:48.638 --> 00:00:52.119
It's the tallest stone statue ever built in ancient Egypt.

12
00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:59.373
Scientists believe it was created around 2500 BC, maybe during Pharaoh Khafre's reign.

13
00:01:00.294 --> 00:01:04.977
Carved from limestone, the statue has a lion's body and a person's head.

14
00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:13.502
The Great Sphinx really is "great"; its massive body is about 73 meters long and 20 meters high.

15
00:01:14.662 --> 00:01:20.966
Its head is bigger than a mansion, and its body weighs about the same as fifty jumbo jets!

16
00:01:22.027 --> 00:01:27.389
The sphinx, a mythological creature, first appeared in ancient Egyptian and Greek culture.

17
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.632
In art and stories, the sphinx always has a lion's body and a human's face.

18
00:01:33.832 --> 00:01:40.975
But while the ancient Greeks portrayed the sphinx as female, usually with wings, the ancient Egyptians portrayed the

19
00:01:41.035 --> 00:01:41.996
sphinx as male.

20
00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:50.720
Many Egyptian temples and pyramids have sphinx statues standing guard; the ancient Egyptians probably saw them as benevolent

21
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:57.996
protectors. The appearance of the sphinx in culture has given scientists clues about the Great Sphinx monument.

22
00:01:59.177 --> 00:02:01.118
But many mysteries still surround it.

23
00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:05.661
For instance, scholars wonder about the Sphinx's face.

24
00:02:06.802 --> 00:02:08.603
Was it carved to look like a real person?

25
00:02:09.023 --> 00:02:12.326
Perhaps Pharaoh Khafre or his father, Pharaoh Khufu?

26
00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.729
Many experts suspect the Sphinx has Khafre's face.

27
00:02:17.769 --> 00:02:21.552
That's because Khafre had a beard, and so did the statue, originally.

28
00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:24.309
Why was the statue built?

29
00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:29.952
Maybe it was constructed to honor the pharaoh—a symbol of his awesome power.

30
00:02:30.932 --> 00:02:34.194
Or perhaps it was put there, facing east, to worship the sun.

31
00:02:35.194 --> 00:02:40.557
In ancient Egypt, the horizon was believed to be where the dead entered the afterlife.

32
00:02:41.577 --> 00:02:44.298
The Great Sphinx could be guarding that sacred spot.

33
00:02:45.539 --> 00:02:47.480
And who built the Great Sphinx?

34
00:02:48.576 --> 00:02:55.539
While the nearby pyramids have inscriptions and clues about their builders, the Great Sphinx reveals almost no clues.

35
00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:01.162
Scientists think it was created by the same team that constructed one of the pyramids.

36
00:03:02.122 --> 00:03:07.405
But since these pyramids were built at different times, it's hard to know for sure which team that

37
00:03:07.465 --> 00:03:14.048
was. And here's another mystery about the Sphinx's construction—it was never finished.

38
00:03:15.132 --> 00:03:20.657
Scholars don't know why, but the builders seem to have abandoned the project shortly before its completion.

39
00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:26.962
I was surprised to learn this, but sand has buried the Great Sphinx on and off throughout most

40
00:03:27.022 --> 00:03:28.063
of its existence.

41
00:03:29.364 --> 00:03:35.789
According to a story from around 1400 BC, a prince was hunting in the hot desert and saw

42
00:03:35.829 --> 00:03:37.971
the Sphinx's head sticking out of the sand.

43
00:03:38.992 --> 00:03:41.374
He decided to sit in the shade under the head.

44
00:03:42.295 --> 00:03:48.709
The prince fell asleep, and when the sun reached its highest point, the statue appeared to the prince

45
00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:49.470
in a dream.

46
00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:55.911
It said that if the prince uncovered the rest of the statue, the prince would become the next

47
00:03:56.111 --> 00:04:02.993
pharaoh. The prince did as the statue said, and he became King Thutmose IV!

48
00:04:04.294 --> 00:04:08.815
Oh, and over time the Great Sphinx was buried under sand again, of course!

49
00:04:09.755 --> 00:04:13.056
Being buried under the sand may have helped to protect the Sphinx.

50
00:04:14.176 --> 00:04:19.339
If the Sphinx had not been buried for most of its existence, it would have disappeared long ago.

51
00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.102
Still, the statue has suffered a lot of damage over time.

52
00:04:25.102 --> 00:04:29.785
Its nose is missing—gone forever, probably chiseled out by looters.

53
00:04:30.505 --> 00:04:31.906
But that's not the worst problem.

54
00:04:32.827 --> 00:04:35.628
The statue is slowly turning to dust!

55
00:04:36.749 --> 00:04:41.772
Limestone is soft, and wind, water, and sand have weakened the statue over time.

56
00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.442
Two more recent threats to the Great Sphinx are pollution and rising groundwater.

57
00:04:48.303 --> 00:04:53.125
Today the stone is treated with special chemicals that help protect it from the pollution.

58
00:04:54.086 --> 00:04:59.028
And holes have been drilled in several spots near the statue to prevent water damage.

59
00:05:00.068 --> 00:05:07.092
Luckily, scientists also used sophisticated laser scanning equipment to closely examine the statue.

60
00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:14.754
The equipment helped to identify its weak spots, and now scientists can take steps to limit future damage.

61
00:05:15.895 --> 00:05:22.400
Thousands of years ago, as the Great Sphinx sat here, gazing at the rising sun, it was probably

62
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.842
guarding the pharaohs' entryway to the afterlife.

63
00:05:25.903 --> 00:05:27.885
Now it's our time to be the guards.

64
00:05:28.466 --> 00:05:32.829
We have to watch the ancient Sphinx carefully and take good care of it.

65
00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:38.831
That way, thousands of years from now, people will still be admiring its beauty.
